./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1tnjlu/TASK-260715-1tnjlu_spawn-log_-analyst--solution-architect--codex-.log:6118:/bin/zsh -lc "task-board m 'create(type=task, parent=STORY-260715-2bfjhn, name=establish-evidence-gated-dns-runtime-limits, title=\"Establish evidence-gated DNS profile and runtime limits\", description=\"Produce the accountable evidence decision for every numeric DNS value deliberately deferred by ADR-022 so production profile validation and DNS transports receive one versioned injected policy rather than unevidenced constants.\", scope=\"In scope: maximum configured endpoint count; DNS TCP message and framing bytes; per-query reservation and aggregate DNS memory accounting; in-flight and queued-byte capacities; SSH channel-open, response, logical-query, startup-readiness, and idle-close timing; structural M1 endpoint-attempt and M2 UDP-to-TCP accounting; controlled IPv4/IPv6/loopback/unreachable resolver fixtures; extension memory and startup budgets; validation relationships; defaults, hard caps, revalidation triggers, and downstream handoff updates. Out of scope: choosing a resolver vendor, changing explicit numeric dns53 identity, implementing the DNS listener/upstream/cache/relay, profile UI, physical-resolver fallback, DoH, discovery, and production code work beyond a disposable measurement harness.\", ac=\"1. A TASK-ID-scoped evidence report compares candidate endpoint cardinalities, message sizes, capacities, byte budgets, and timing values against primary DNS/SSH requirements, the accepted runtime memory/startup contracts, and repeatable controlled-fixture measurements. 2. The selected DNSRuntimePolicyV1 names exact injectable production defaults and validation ceilings for endpoint count, maximum DNS message bytes, in-flight queries, queued and aggregate bytes, channel-open/response/logical/startup/idle timing, and proves all cross-field relationships; no value is stored in the user profile unless ADR-022 requires it. 3. Worst-case accounting reserves request, maximum response, framing, correlation metadata, connection buffers, retry batch, and queued bytes within an explicit DNS component budget; inconsistent policies fail validation and measurements record peak footprint and cleanup. 4. Reliability evidence covers IPv4-only, IPv6-only, dual ordered, loopback, unreachable/malformed/stalling endpoints, concurrent connection failure, cancellation, and M2 one-UDP-plus-bounded-TCP semantics with no physical resolver access. 5. An independent architecture reviewer accepts the values and revalidation triggers, and the task updates ADR-022, routing/DNS source of truth, test vectors, and concrete downstream task resources before production composition or profile UX consumes defaults.\"'" in /Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel
