./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-100wu6/TASK-260720-100wu6_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:696:Materialize the candidate-neutral SSH transport contract IN CODE in ReluxTunnelCore, realizing the reviewed TASK-260715-2ny6z4 design contract (585-line doc + diagrams — authoritative). This is the shared boundary BOTH adapters (TASK-260715-1af33i NIOSSH, 1ozsb6 libssh2) and the conformance suite (2d3g5e) compile against; it must land BEFORE them. Extend Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHContracts.swift (currently a skeleton). REQUIREMENTS (AC-aligned): (1) ReluxTunnelCore exposes the COMPLETE candidate-neutral interface WITHOUT importing/naming ReluxNIOSSH, SwiftNIO, libssh2, OpenSSL, or any adapter type (preserve check-core-boundaries); (2) types force raw host-key bytes + algorithm + SHA-256 fingerprint into policy input BEFORE credential access/auth, and represent every host/auth outcome; (3) direct-tcpip + exec channels expose bounded partial writes (writeSome), reads, stdout/stderr + exit results, EOF/half-close, reset, cancel, idempotent close, exec-stdin upload, and independently observable CAPPED receive windows (snapshot + cap per section 9); (4) injected clock + policy types expose automatic byte/time rekey, explicit production-path trigger, server rekey, keepalive, cancellation/timeouts, typed events, schema-v1 privacy-safe metrics exactly as the contract defines (section 10 + 12 + 13); (5) Swift Testing fixtures verify invalid states, policy validation, candidate-type erasure, stable error mapping/data shape, metric/event schema, and secret/destination/command EXCLUSION from logs. Candidate-type erasure = the core defines the protocol/factory/dependencies so adapters plug in without the core naming them. Build + boundary checks + swift test pass on macOS. Contract CODE only (no engine/adapter here).
