# TASK-260728-yx2fca reviewer verdict

## Verdict

Changes requested. Route: to-dev. This is bounded implementation rework, not Stop-The-Line.

## P1 finding: reported receive-window policy can violate its immutable cap

SSHChannelPolicy stores initialReceiveWindowBytes independently from consumerReceiveWindowCredit and validates only positivity at Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHContracts.swift:871. SSHConsumerReceiveWindowPolicy validates a separate initialReceiveWindowBytes argument against its cap at line 908 but discards that value. A caller can therefore construct a reported policy using initial 8 and cap 8, then embed it in SSHChannelPolicy with initial 9. The resulting public value claims exact reported consumer-credit semantics while its advertised initial window exceeds its immutable cap. This contradicts the exact M3 semantic and the seam validation model. Existing tests validate only each initializer separately and do not cover the cross-object mismatch.

Required rework: make the reported policy self-consistent by validating SSHChannelPolicy.initialReceiveWindowBytes against the reported maximumAdvertisedReceiveWindowBytes, or remove the duplicated initial value and make one policy own it. Add a regression proving a reported initial-greater-than-cap combination fails while notReported and unsupported viability states remain constructible. Update LOGBOOK.md and this outcome, then rerun focused tests, formatting, diff check, boundary check, and make validate-core.

## Verified evidence

Contract and consumer mapping are otherwise accepted: the contract exhaustively classifies 16 M0 mandatory requirements and four M3 deferred semantics owned by TASK-260728-3cveay; seven canonical and board copies are byte-identical at SHA-256 87892d6e2269d394dea6b3f5c18aad3b2a1d957fe5d474459ea0d8dc4317e775; all three consumers reference the M0 viability tier; retained libssh2 and ReluxNIOSSH blocker artifacts remain attached; no SSH diagrams-as-code require revision. The prior channel-open reason defect is fixed with a nonoptional validated state.

